<Placemark><name>Mathews Cemetery (John Mathews lead)</name><description>Exact spot

Mathews Cemetery near Chadwick, Christian County (USGS coordinates).

UNCONFIRMED LEAD. John Mathews was the third Bald Knobber hanged in 1889, and the Christian County group was centered on Chadwick. I found no source saying where he is buried. This family cemetery is a lead, not a match.

Access: Likely private land.

Sources:
Bald Knobbers (Wikipedia): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bald_Knobbers</description><styleUrl>#exact</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.031830,36.925390</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Snapp Balds: Bald Knobbers' first meeting place</name><description>Approximate area, 0.5 mi radius

Just north of Kirbyville, Taney County. USGS marks Snapp Balds as a ridge range; the exact meeting knob isn't pinned.

Where Nat Kinney's Taney County vigilantes first met. The open bald knobs let them watch for spies, and gave the group its name.

Access: Private land likely.

Sources:
Bald Knobbers (Wikipedia): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bald_Knobbers</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.174900,36.638400</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
