<Placemark><name>Clark's Mill battle &amp; blockhouse</name><description>Approximate area, 0.6 mi radius

On Bryant Creek about a mile north of Vera Cruz, Douglas County. Placed from that description.

Union blockhouse captured and destroyed in the Nov. 7, 1862 battle. A 2012 report says traces of the old Vera Cruz Road are still visible on the farm. Good LiDAR target.

Access: PRIVATE farm.

Sources:
Battle of Clark's Mill (Wikipedia): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Clark%27s_Mill
KSMU: landowner finds his farm was a battle site (2012): https://www.ksmu.org/local-history/2012-09-27/what-do-you-do-upon-discovering-your-land-was-a-civil-war-battle-site-host-a-reenactment-naturally</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.493500,36.928400</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
