<Placemark><name>Alf Bolin's treasure cave</name><description>Approximate area, 0.6 mi radius

Fox Creek Hills, Section 20, T22N R20W, about 2 miles southwest of the old Mincy store and mill, Taney County. Circle is that section's center.

Bolin's loot is said to be buried near a cave in these hills. A stranger spent several summers searching from a farm on Highway JJ and never said whether he found it.

Access: Ownership not checked. Confirm before going.

Sources:
White River Valley Hist. Quarterly: Alf Bolin's Buried Treasure (1974): https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V5/n6/w74a.html</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.126300,36.541330</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
