<Placemark><name>Murder Rocks Union soldiers' graves</name><description>Approximate area, 0.9 mi radius

About 3 miles south of Kirbyville, on what was the Charley Mahnkey place in 1974, Taney County. Circle placed from distance only.

Two Union soldiers ambushed at Murder Rocks were buried here. No marker is described.

Access: Private land.

Sources:
White River Valley Hist. Quarterly: Alf Bolin's Buried Treasure (1974): https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V5/n6/w74a.html</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.164100,36.579600</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
