<Placemark><name>Smallett Cave: the Headless Cobbler</name><description>Approximate area, 1.6 mi radius

Near Smallett, Douglas County. Spring Creek runs just north of the cave mouth, close to the Glade Top Trail. Circle is centered on Smallett.

A Civil War cobbler, believed to be Wesley Evans, hid in the cave to work out of sight of bushwhackers. People report a headless figure on the back roads at dusk, tapping inside the cave, a red light, and phantom horses.

Access: Ownership unknown; nearby road may be private.

Sources:
Ozarks Alive: Headless Cobbler of Smallett Cave: https://www.ozarksalive.com/stories/headlesscobblersmallettcave</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.714100,36.848700</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
