<Placemark><name>Blue Man of Spring Creek: 1865 sighting</name><description>Approximate area, 0.9 mi radius

North slope of 'Upper Twin Mountain', site of the first sighting in 1865. Pinned on USGS Twin Mountain (Howell County, near the Douglas line). Likely the same mountain but NOT confirmed.

Hairy wild man said to roam the Spring Creek, North Fork and Indian Creek hills from the 1860s. A 1911 posse reportedly found his den full of animal bones. Its location was never recorded.

Access: Ownership not checked.

Sources:
Ozarks Alive: The Blue Man: https://www.ozarksalive.com/stories/blue-man-ozarks-legend-long-told-nearly-forgotten
Howell County News: When the Blue Man roamed: https://www.howellcountynews.com/history/when-blue-man-roamed-howell-county</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.087100,36.941400</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
