<Placemark><name>Garrison Cave: treasure &amp; skeleton</name><description>Approximate area, 0.7 mi radius

About 1 mile east of Ozark, below the old Garrison homestead on a hilltop near a bluff, Christian County. Circle placed from that description.

In 1853 a stranger with a divining rod said treasure was buried in the cave. Diggers quit twice over ghostly sounds. A later dig found ashes, slag, bones and a human skeleton, but no treasure.

Access: Unknown. Ownership not checked.

Sources:
Ozarks' History: Gold in Ozark Hills (1893 article): https://ozarkshistory.blogspot.com/2011/04/gold-in-ozark-hills.html</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.187900,37.020900</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
