<Placemark><name>Dewey's lost lead cave</name><description>Approximate area, 0.7 mi radius

Side of Dewey Bald, just east of the Stone–Taney line (USGS summit coordinates; the cave's side of the mountain isn't given). The summit itself is now developed.

Captain Sam Dewey, a hermit and government agent among the Delaware, supposedly mined nearly pure lead from a cave here. He hid the entrance under a flat rock covered with dirt. The 1923 writer hunted for it as a boy and never found it. A burned cabin site was said to be on top.

Access: Mostly private land. Ownership not checked.

Sources:
WRV Quarterly: Waldo Powell, Dewey Bald Legend (1923, reprinted 1978): https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V6/N7/Sp78g.htm</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.296010,36.655060</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
