<Placemark><name>Table Rock Bluff blockhouse</name><description>Approximate area, 0.5 mi radius

Table Rock bluff near the mouth of Fall Creek on the White River, Taney County (USGS 'Table Rock' summit). Settlers also smelted lead at Slick Rock Ford on Fall Creek.

Settlers reportedly built blockhouses on a narrow point of this bluff, with a spring inside, as a fort in case of trouble with the Delaware. Barricade lines or building pads could show on LiDAR if the story is true.

Access: Near Table Rock Dam; ownership not checked.

Sources:
WRV Quarterly: Dewey Bald Legend: https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V6/N7/Sp78g.htm</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.280260,36.591890</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
