<Placemark><name>Kirbyville picnic spring shootout</name><description>Approximate area, 0.6 mi radius

A spring at the Kirbyville picnic ground, Taney County. Circle is centered on Kirbyville; the spring isn't located.

July 4, 1889: the Miles brothers shot Sheriff Galba Branson and detective Ed Funk in front of about 100 picnickers, then escaped into the brush. The fallout from the Bald Knobber era.

Access: Unknown.

Sources:
WRV Quarterly: Willful Murder (1889 news reprint): https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V5/N12/s76e.html
Bald Knobbers (Wikipedia): https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bald_Knobbers</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.164070,36.623120</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
