<Placemark><name>Yocum silver &amp; the 'Spanish fort'</name><description>Approximate area, 5.0 mi radius

Galena / lower James River area, Stone County. Very wide circle: no source gives a usable spot.

Legend says Spaniards cached silver in caves here and the Yocum family later minted 'Yocum dollars' from it. One searcher claimed to find foundation stones of a small Spanish fort; another found a rock painting of a human figure on a creek bed. Historians doubt the whole story.

Access: Lower areas are under Table Rock Lake.

Sources:
WRV Quarterly: Legendary Hidden Silver (1978): https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V6/N9/F78i.htm
WRV Quarterly: Yocum Silver Dollar, Fact or Legend?: https://sgcld.thelibrary.org/lochist/periodicals/wrv/V7/N11/Sp82g.htm</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.466600,36.805300</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
