<Placemark><name>Brown's Cave &amp; the 'Devil's Gulch'</name><description>Approximate area, 0.9 mi radius

Bryant Creek about 2 miles downstream from the mouth of Rippee Creek, about 6 miles from Vera Cruz, Douglas County. Placed from that description. Entrance is 20–30 ft above the creek on a steep, rugged hill.

A big cave that a 1957 county history says was never fully explored. A second section about 1.5 miles in has a deep chasm called the 'Devil's Gulch.' Methodists held meetings inside in 1892, and old-timers told stories about it.

Access: Ownership not checked. Rippee State Wildlife Management Area (USGS name) is nearby; check the boundary.

Sources:
Reminiscent History of Douglas County, 1857–1957 (Missouri Digital Heritage): https://mdh.contentdm.oclc.org/digital/collection/mocohist/id/7190
Dr. Brown's Excerpts of the Douglas County Herald, 1887–99 (PDF): http://www.theozarkuncle.com/Documents-Digital/Excerpts-1887-99.pdf</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.471000,36.843000</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
