<Placemark><name>Fort Lawrence (Beaver Station)</name><description>Approximate area, 0.5 mi radius

Beaver Creek at Rome, Douglas County. Built to guard Lawrence Mill. Circle centered on Rome.

Union militia blockhouse guarding the mill and the Forsyth road. Confederates under Emmett McDonald surprised and burned it on Jan. 7, 1863, the day before the Battle of Springfield. Family legend says a log cabin from the fort was moved to Ava.

Access: Ownership not checked.

Sources:
