<Placemark><name>Thornfield 'volcano' cave (1899)</name><description>Approximate area, 0.7 mi radius

Bill Trent's farm, about 2 miles north of Thornfield, Ozark County. Placed from that distance.

In 1899 smoke poured out of a plowed field for three days. A hole had blown open, and men who went in found a large cave in what looked like a bed of onyx. Cause never explained in the paper.

Access: Private farmland.

Sources:
Dr. Brown's Excerpts of the Douglas County Herald, 1887–99 (PDF): http://www.theozarkuncle.com/Documents-Digital/Excerpts-1887-99.pdf</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.659300,36.737700</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
