<Placemark><name>Indian money cave, Clay Township</name><description>Approximate area, 3.7 mi radius

Somewhere in Clay Township, northeastern Douglas County. Very wide circle centered on the township.

An 1892 Herald correspondent wrote that an old Indian came through saying his tribe had hidden a large amount of money in a cave here. The writer joked that if you don't find the money you might find lead.

Access: Mostly private land.

Sources:
Dr. Brown's Excerpts of the Douglas County Herald, 1887–99 (PDF): http://www.theozarkuncle.com/Documents-Digital/Excerpts-1887-99.pdf</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.469500,37.019200</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
