<Placemark><name>Pennington's lead mine</name><description>Approximate area, 0.5 mi radius

About 2 miles east of Ava, Douglas County. Placed from that distance.

Capt. E. D. Pennington leased out his lead mine here in the 1890s. Old shafts and spoil piles are good LiDAR targets. Not a legend, but a forgotten site.

Access: Private land likely. Old shafts are dangerous.

Sources:
Dr. Brown's Excerpts of the Douglas County Herald, 1887–99 (PDF): http://www.theozarkuncle.com/Documents-Digital/Excerpts-1887-99.pdf</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.624000,36.952000</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
