<Placemark><name>Jordan Creek sealed Spanish cave</name><description>Approximate area, 0.6 mi radius

Jordan Creek near where it joins a larger creek, Springfield (pinned at USGS Jordan Creek mouth). Railroad construction reportedly sealed the entrance.

1858 letters and maps described a cave sealed with a flat stone marked with a turkey track, holding Spanish bullion. People dug for decades into the 1930s.

Access: Urban/private land.

Sources:
Ozarks First: The long hunt for hidden gold and treasure in the Ozarks: https://www.ozarksfirst.com/news/ozarks-treasure-hunting-obsession/</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.326600,37.187500</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
