<Placemark><name>Ash Cave: Civil War gold</name><description>Approximate area, 3.7 mi radius

Near Cassville, Barry County. Cave not located; wide circle centered on Cassville.

Gold said to be hidden from bushwhackers, or stolen from a stagecoach on the Old Wire Road. 1920s diggers went 25–30 ft into crevices and found only arrowheads.

Access: Ownership not checked.

Sources:
Ozarks First: The long hunt for hidden gold and treasure in the Ozarks: https://www.ozarksfirst.com/news/ozarks-treasure-hunting-obsession/</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-93.868800,36.677000</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
