<Placemark><name>Bussman Lodge ruins</name><description>Exact spot

Along the river near Devil's Elbow, Pulaski County. Coordinates come from a 2014 explorer report you supplied; I couldn't open that report to double-check them. Access road starts near 37.8203, -92.0558 and is about a 1-mile walk.

Retreat built for Cooper-Bussman Fuse Co. employees, later used by Boy Scouts. Reported remains: two lodge chimneys, concrete bait reservoirs, a spring house, garage foundation, rock bridge and old dock.

Access: Mark Twain National Forest per a 2003 geocache listing. Road is rough; 4WD or walk in. ATVs need a permit.

Sources:
Geocache GCG5RT: Bussman Lodge (archived): https://www.geocaching.com/geocache/GCG5RT</description><styleUrl>#exact</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.074170,37.824400</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
<Placemark><name>Mayfield settlement ruins</name><description>Approximate area, 0.7 mi radius

Around Mayfield Cemetery south of Devil's Elbow, Pulaski County (USGS cemetery coordinates). Scattered ruins and the Mayfield cliffs are reported nearby.

A former settlement that explorers report as scattered ruins plus a cemetery. Little or nothing may be left above ground in places. Building pads and old roads should show on LiDAR.

Access: Not checked. This area may be on or near Fort Leonard Wood land; confirm before going.

Sources:
Mayfield Cemetery (USGS GNIS): https://edits.nationalmap.gov/apps/gaz-domestic/public/search/names</description><styleUrl>#area</styleUrl><Point><coordinates>-92.066540,37.785310</coordinates></Point></Placemark>
